                  <td>Set Less Than (Signed comparison). Writes 1 to rd if rs1 is smaller in signed two's complement.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr data-cat="alu-reg">
                  <td><code>sltu rd, rs1, rs2</code></td>
                  <td><span class="fmt-badge fmt-r">R-Type</span></td>
                  <td><code>0110011 (0x33)</code></td>
                  <td><code>011 (0x3)</code></td>
                  <td><code>0000000 (0x00)</code></td>
                  <td><code>R[rd] &larr; (R[rs1] &lt;u R[rs2]) ? 1 : 0</code></td>
                  <td><span class="status-badge ok">✓ Valid (x0..x15)</span></td>
                  <td>Set Less Than Unsigned. Synthesizes boolean test <code>snez rd, rs</code> via <code>sltu rd, x0, rs</code>.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr data-cat="alu-reg">
                  <td><code>xor rd, rs1, rs2</code></td>
                  <td><span class="fmt-badge fmt-r">R-Type</span></td>
                  <td><code>0110011 (0x33)</code></td>
                  <td><code>100 (0x4)</code></td>
                  <td><code>0000000 (0x00)</code></td>
                  <td><code>R[rd] &larr; R[rs1] ^ R[rs2]</code></td>
                  <td><span class="status-badge ok">✓ Valid (x0..x15)</span></td>
                  <td>Bitwise Exclusive-OR across all 32 bit positions. Zero carry propagation delay.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr data-cat="alu-reg">
                  <td><code>srl rd, rs1, rs2</code></td>
                  <td><span class="fmt-badge fmt-r">R-Type</span></td>
                  <td><code>0110011 (0x33)</code></td>
                  <td><code>101 (0x5)</code></td>
                  <td><code>0000000 (0x00)</code></td>
                  <td><code>R[rd] &larr; R[rs1] &gt;&gt;&gt; R[rs2][4:0]</code></td>
                  <td><span class="status-badge ok">✓ Valid (x0..x15)</span></td>
                  <td>Shift Right Logical. Shifts right by rs2[4:0] bits, filling vacant upper bits with 0.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr data-cat="alu-reg">
                  <td><code>sra rd, rs1, rs2</code></td>
                  <td><span class="fmt-badge fmt-r">R-Type</span></td>
                  <td><code>0110011 (0x33)</code></td>
                  <td><code>101 (0x5)</code></td>
                  <td><code>0100000 (0x20)</code></td>
                  <td><code>R[rd] &larr; R[rs1] &gt;&gt; R[rs2][4:0]</code></td>
                  <td><span class="status-badge ok">✓ Valid (x0..x15)</span></td>
                  <td>Shift Right Arithmetic. Shifts right by rs2[4:0] bits, replicating sign bit (rs1[31]).</td>
                </tr>
                <tr data-cat="alu-reg">
                  <td><code>or rd, rs1, rs2</code></td>
                  <td><span class="fmt-badge fmt-r">R-Type</span></td>
                  <td><code>0110011 (0x33)</code></td>
                  <td><code>110 (0x6)</code></td>
                  <td><code>0000000 (0x00)</code></td>
                  <td><code>R[rd] &larr; R[rs1] | R[rs2]</code></td>
                  <td><span class="status-badge ok">✓ Valid (x0..x15)</span></td>
                  <td>Bitwise OR across all 32 bit positions. Simple combinational gate layer.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr data-cat="alu-reg">
                  <td><code>and rd, rs1, rs2</code></td>
                  <td><span class="fmt-badge fmt-r">R-Type</span></td>
                  <td><code>0110011 (0x33)</code></td>
                  <td><code>111 (0x7)</code></td>
                  <td><code>0000000 (0x00)</code></td>
                  <td><code>R[rd] &larr; R[rs1] &amp; R[rs2]</code></td>
                  <td><span class="status-badge ok">✓ Valid (x0..x15)</span></td>
                  <td>Bitwise AND across all 32 bit positions. Used for bit-masking operations.</td>
                </tr>

                <!-- 9 I-Type ALU Instructions -->
                <tr data-cat="alu-imm">
                  <td><code>addi rd, rs1, imm</code></td>
                  <td><span class="fmt-badge fmt-i">I-Type</span></td>
                  <td><code>0010011 (0x13)</code></td>
                  <td><code>000 (0x0)</code></td>
                  <td><code>imm[11:0] (sign-ext)</code></td>
                  <td><code>R[rd] &larr; R[rs1] + sext(imm[11:0])</code></td>
                  <td><span class="status-badge ok">✓ Valid (x0..x15)</span></td>
                  <td>Add 12-bit signed immediate (-2048..+2047). Synthesizes <code>nop</code> (<code>addi x0, x0, 0</code>) and <code>mv rd, rs</code>.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr data-cat="alu-imm">
                  <td><code>slti rd, rs1, imm</code></td>
                  <td><span class="fmt-badge fmt-i">I-Type</span></td>
                  <td><code>0010011 (0x13)</code></td>
                  <td><code>010 (0x2)</code></td>
                  <td><code>imm[11:0] (sign-ext)</code></td>
                  <td><code>R[rd] &larr; (R[rs1] &lt;s sext(imm)) ? 1 : 0</code></td>
                  <td><span class="status-badge ok">✓ Valid (x0..x15)</span></td>
                  <td>Set Less Than Immediate (Signed). Compares rs1 against sign-extended 12-bit immediate.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr data-cat="alu-imm">
                  <td><code>sltiu rd, rs1, imm</code></td>
                  <td><span class="fmt-badge fmt-i">I-Type</span></td>
                  <td><code>0010011 (0x13)</code></td>
                  <td><code>011 (0x3)</code></td>
                  <td><code>imm[11:0] (sign-ext)</code></td>
                  <td><code>R[rd] &larr; (R[rs1] &lt;u sext(imm)) ? 1 : 0</code></td>
                  <td><span class="status-badge ok">✓ Valid (x0..x15)</span></td>
                  <td>Set Less Than Immediate Unsigned. Synthesizes <code>seqz rd, rs</code> (<code>sltiu rd, rs, 1</code>).</td>
                </tr>
                <tr data-cat="alu-imm">
                  <td><code>xori rd, rs1, imm</code></td>
                  <td><span class="fmt-badge fmt-i">I-Type</span></td>
                  <td><code>0010011 (0x13)</code></td>
                  <td><code>100 (0x4)</code></td>
                  <td><code>imm[11:0] (sign-ext)</code></td>
                  <td><code>R[rd] &larr; R[rs1] ^ sext(imm)</code></td>
                  <td><span class="status-badge ok">✓ Valid (x0..x15)</span></td>
                  <td>Bitwise XOR with 12-bit signed immediate. Synthesizes bitwise NOT (<code>xori rd, rs, -1</code>).</td>
                </tr>
                <tr data-cat="alu-imm">
                  <td><code>ori rd, rs1, imm</code></td>
                  <td><span class="fmt-badge fmt-i">I-Type</span></td>
                  <td><code>0010011 (0x13)</code></td>
                  <td><code>110 (0x6)</code></td>
                  <td><code>imm[11:0] (sign-ext)</code></td>
                  <td><code>R[rd] &larr; R[rs1] | sext(imm)</code></td>
                  <td><span class="status-badge ok">✓ Valid (x0..x15)</span></td>
                  <td>Bitwise OR with 12-bit signed immediate. Used to set constant bitflags.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr data-cat="alu-imm">
                  <td><code>andi rd, rs1, imm</code></td>
                  <td><span class="fmt-badge fmt-i">I-Type</span></td>
                  <td><code>0010011 (0x13)</code></td>
                  <td><code>111 (0x7)</code></td>
                  <td><code>imm[11:0] (sign-ext)</code></td>
                  <td><code>R[rd] &larr; R[rs1] &amp; sext(imm)</code></td>
                  <td><span class="status-badge ok">✓ Valid (x0..x15)</span></td>
                  <td>Bitwise AND with 12-bit signed immediate. Used to mask bitfields.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr data-cat="alu-imm">
                  <td><code>slli rd, rs1, shamt</code></td>
                  <td><span class="fmt-badge fmt-i">I-Type</span></td>
                  <td><code>0010011 (0x13)</code></td>
                  <td><code>001 (0x1)</code></td>
                  <td><code>imm[11:5] = 0000000</code></td>
                  <td><code>R[rd] &larr; R[rs1] &lt;&lt; shamt[4:0]</code></td>
                  <td><span class="status-badge ok">✓ Valid (x0..x15)</span></td>
                  <td>Shift Left Logical Immediate (0..31 bits). <code>shamt</code> encoded in bits [24:20].</td>
                </tr>
                <tr data-cat="alu-imm">
                  <td><code>srli rd, rs1, shamt</code></td>
                  <td><span class="fmt-badge fmt-i">I-Type</span></td>
                  <td><code>0010011 (0x13)</code></td>
                  <td><code>101 (0x5)</code></td>
                  <td><code>imm[11:5] = 0000000</code></td>
                  <td><code>R[rd] &larr; R[rs1] &gt;&gt;&gt; shamt[4:0]</code></td>
                  <td><span class="status-badge ok">✓ Valid (x0..x15)</span></td>
                  <td>Shift Right Logical Immediate (0..31 bits). Zero fill into upper vacated bit positions.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr data-cat="alu-imm">
                  <td><code>srai rd, rs1, shamt</code></td>
                  <td><span class="fmt-badge fmt-i">I-Type</span></td>
                  <td><code>0010011 (0x13)</code></td>
                  <td><code>101 (0x5)</code></td>
                  <td><code>imm[11:5] = 0100000</code></td>
                  <td><code>R[rd] &larr; R[rs1] &gt;&gt; shamt[4:0]</code></td>
                  <td><span class="status-badge ok">✓ Valid (x0..x15)</span></td>
                  <td>Shift Right Arithmetic Immediate. Preserves sign bit across division by powers of 2.</td>
                </tr>

                <!-- 2 U-Type Instructions -->
                <tr data-cat="upper-imm">
                  <td><code>lui rd, imm</code></td>
                  <td><span class="fmt-badge fmt-u">U-Type</span></td>
                  <td><code>0110111 (0x37)</code></td>
                  <td>&mdash;</td>
                  <td><code>imm[31:12] (20-bit)</code></td>
                  <td><code>R[rd] &larr; imm[31:12] &lt;&lt; 12</code></td>
                  <td><span class="status-badge ok">✓ Valid (x0..x15)</span></td>
                  <td>Load Upper Immediate. Writes 20-bit immediate into bits [31:12], zeroes lower 12 bits. Paired with <code>addi</code> to construct 32-bit constants.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr data-cat="upper-imm">
                  <td><code>auipc rd, imm</code></td>
                  <td><span class="fmt-badge fmt-u">U-Type</span></td>
                  <td><code>0010111 (0x17)</code></td>
                  <td>&mdash;</td>
                  <td><code>imm[31:12] (20-bit)</code></td>
                  <td><code>R[rd] &larr; PC + (imm[31:12] &lt;&lt; 12)</code></td>
                  <td><span class="status-badge ok">✓ Valid (x0..x15)</span></td>
                  <td>Add Upper Immediate to PC. Forms PC-relative addresses; essential for Position-Independent Code (PIC) and long jumps.</td>
                </tr>

                <!-- 2 Unconditional Jumps -->
                <tr data-cat="jumps">
                  <td><code>jal rd, offset</code></td>
                  <td><span class="fmt-badge fmt-j">J-Type</span></td>
                  <td><code>1101111 (0x6F)</code></td>
                  <td>&mdash;</td>
                  <td><code>imm[20|10:1|11|19:12]</code></td>
                  <td><code>R[rd] &larr; PC + 4; PC &larr; PC + sext(offset)</code></td>
                  <td><span class="status-badge ok">✓ Valid (x0..x15)</span></td>
                  <td>Jump and Link (±1 MB range). Saves return PC in rd. Synthesizes unconditional jump <code>j</code> (<code>rd=x0</code>) and <code>call</code> (<code>rd=ra</code>).</td>
                </tr>
                <tr data-cat="jumps">
                  <td><code>jalr rd, rs1, offset</code></td>
                  <td><span class="fmt-badge fmt-i">I-Type</span></td>
                  <td><code>1100111 (0x67)</code></td>
                  <td><code>000 (0x0)</code></td>
                  <td><code>imm[11:0] (sign-ext)</code></td>
                  <td><code>t = PC + 4; PC = (R[rs1] + sext(offset)) &amp; ~1; R[rd] = t</code></td>
                  <td><span class="status-badge ok">✓ Valid (x0..x15)</span></td>
                  <td>Jump and Link Register. Computed indirect jump. Critical for function pointer calls, switch jump tables, and <code>ret</code> (<code>jalr x0, ra, 0</code>).</td>
                </tr>

                <!-- 6 Conditional Branches -->
                <tr data-cat="branches">
                  <td><code>beq rs1, rs2, offset</code></td>
                  <td><span class="fmt-badge fmt-b">B-Type</span></td>
                  <td><code>1100011 (0x63)</code></td>
                  <td><code>000 (0x0)</code></td>
                  <td><code>imm[12|10:5|4:1|11]</code></td>
                  <td><code>if (R[rs1] == R[rs2]) PC &larr; PC + sext(offset)</code></td>
                  <td><span class="status-badge ok">✓ Valid (x0..x15)</span></td>
                  <td>Branch if Equal (±4 KB PC-relative displacement). Synthesizes <code>beqz rs, offset</code> (<code>beq rs, x0, offset</code>).</td>
                </tr>
                <tr data-cat="branches">
                  <td><code>bne rs1, rs2, offset</code></td>
                  <td><span class="fmt-badge fmt-b">B-Type</span></td>
                  <td><code>1100011 (0x63)</code></td>
                  <td><code>001 (0x1)</code></td>
                  <td><code>imm[12|10:5|4:1|11]</code></td>
                  <td><code>if (R[rs1] != R[rs2]) PC &larr; PC + sext(offset)</code></td>
                  <td><span class="status-badge ok">✓ Valid (x0..x15)</span></td>
                  <td>Branch if Not Equal. Synthesizes <code>bnez rs, offset</code> (<code>bne rs, x0, offset</code>).</td>
                </tr>
                <tr data-cat="branches">
                  <td><code>blt rs1, rs2, offset</code></td>
                  <td><span class="fmt-badge fmt-b">B-Type</span></td>
                  <td><code>1100011 (0x63)</code></td>
                  <td><code>100 (0x4)</code></td>
                  <td><code>imm[12|10:5|4:1|11]</code></td>
                  <td><code>if (R[rs1] &lt;s R[rs2]) PC &larr; PC + sext(offset)</code></td>
                  <td><span class="status-badge ok">✓ Valid (x0..x15)</span></td>
                  <td>Branch if Less Than (Signed comparison). Synthesizes <code>bltz rs, offset</code> (<code>blt rs, x0, offset</code>).</td>
                </tr>
                <tr data-cat="branches">
                  <td><code>bge rs1, rs2, offset</code></td>
                  <td><span class="fmt-badge fmt-b">B-Type</span></td>
                  <td><code>1100011 (0x63)</code></td>
                  <td><code>101 (0x5)</code></td>
                  <td><code>imm[12|10:5|4:1|11]</code></td>
                  <td><code>if (R[rs1] &gt;=s R[rs2]) PC &larr; PC + sext(offset)</code></td>
                  <td><span class="status-badge ok">✓ Valid (x0..x15)</span></td>
                  <td>Branch if Greater or Equal (Signed). Synthesizes <code>bgez rs, offset</code> (<code>bge rs, x0, offset</code>).</td>
                </tr>
                <tr data-cat="branches">
                  <td><code>bltu rs1, rs2, offset</code></td>
                  <td><span class="fmt-badge fmt-b">B-Type</span></td>
                  <td><code>1100011 (0x63)</code></td>
                  <td><code>110 (0x6)</code></td>
                  <td><code>imm[12|10:5|4:1|11]</code></td>
                  <td><code>if (R[rs1] &lt;u R[rs2]) PC &larr; PC + sext(offset)</code></td>
                  <td><span class="status-badge ok">✓ Valid (x0..x15)</span></td>
                  <td>Branch if Less Than Unsigned. Compares registers as unsigned 32-bit integers.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr data-cat="branches">
                  <td><code>bgeu rs1, rs2, offset</code></td>
                  <td><span class="fmt-badge fmt-b">B-Type</span></td>
                  <td><code>1100011 (0x63)</code></td>
                  <td><code>111 (0x7)</code></td>
                  <td><code>imm[12|10:5|4:1|11]</code></td>
                  <td><code>if (R[rs1] &gt;=u R[rs2]) PC &larr; PC + sext(offset)</code></td>
                  <td><span class="status-badge ok">✓ Valid (x0..x15)</span></td>
                  <td>Branch if Greater or Equal Unsigned. Compares registers as unsigned 32-bit integers.</td>
                </tr>

                <!-- 5 Memory Loads -->
                <tr data-cat="loads">
                  <td><code>lb rd, offset(rs1)</code></td>
                  <td><span class="fmt-badge fmt-i">I-Type</span></td>
                  <td><code>0000011 (0x03)</code></td>
                  <td><code>000 (0x0)</code></td>
                  <td><code>imm[11:0] (sign-ext)</code></td>
                  <td><code>R[rd] &larr; sext(Mem8[R[rs1] + sext(offset)])</code></td>
                  <td><span class="status-badge ok">✓ Valid (x0..x15)</span></td>
                  <td>Load 8-bit Byte from effective address and sign-extend to 32 bits (signed char).</td>
                </tr>
                <tr data-cat="loads">
                  <td><code>lh rd, offset(rs1)</code></td>
                  <td><span class="fmt-badge fmt-i">I-Type</span></td>
                  <td><code>0000011 (0x03)</code></td>
                  <td><code>001 (0x1)</code></td>
                  <td><code>imm[11:0] (sign-ext)</code></td>
                  <td><code>R[rd] &larr; sext(Mem16[R[rs1] + sext(offset)])</code></td>
                  <td><span class="status-badge ok">✓ Valid (x0..x15)</span></td>
                  <td>Load 16-bit Halfword and sign-extend to 32 bits (signed short). Requires halfword alignment.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr data-cat="loads">
                  <td><code>lw rd, offset(rs1)</code></td>
                  <td><span class="fmt-badge fmt-i">I-Type</span></td>
                  <td><code>0000011 (0x03)</code></td>
                  <td><code>010 (0x2)</code></td>
                  <td><code>imm[11:0] (sign-ext)</code></td>
                  <td><code>R[rd] &larr; Mem32[R[rs1] + sext(offset)]</code></td>
                  <td><span class="status-badge ok">✓ Valid (x0..x15)</span></td>
                  <td>Load 32-bit Word directly into destination register. Standard memory read.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr data-cat="loads">
                  <td><code>lbu rd, offset(rs1)</code></td>
                  <td><span class="fmt-badge fmt-i">I-Type</span></td>
                  <td><code>0000011 (0x03)</code></td>
                  <td><code>100 (0x4)</code></td>
                  <td><code>imm[11:0] (sign-ext)</code></td>
                  <td><code>R[rd] &larr; zext(Mem8[R[rs1] + sext(offset)])</code></td>
                  <td><span class="status-badge ok">✓ Valid (x0..x15)</span></td>
                  <td>Load 8-bit Byte and zero-extend to 32 bits (unsigned char / byte stream).</td>
                </tr>
                <tr data-cat="loads">
                  <td><code>lhu rd, offset(rs1)</code></td>
                  <td><span class="fmt-badge fmt-i">I-Type</span></td>
                  <td><code>0000011 (0x03)</code></td>
                  <td><code>101 (0x5)</code></td>
                  <td><code>imm[11:0] (sign-ext)</code></td>
                  <td><code>R[rd] &larr; zext(Mem16[R[rs1] + sext(offset)])</code></td>
                  <td><span class="status-badge ok">✓ Valid (x0..x15)</span></td>
                  <td>Load 16-bit Halfword and zero-extend to 32 bits (unsigned short).</td>
                </tr>

                <!-- 3 Memory Stores -->
                <tr data-cat="stores">
                  <td><code>sb rs2, offset(rs1)</code></td>
                  <td><span class="fmt-badge fmt-s">S-Type</span></td>
                  <td><code>0100011 (0x23)</code></td>
                  <td><code>000 (0x0)</code></td>
                  <td><code>imm[11:5|4:0]</code></td>
                  <td><code>Mem8[R[rs1] + sext(offset)] &larr; R[rs2][7:0]</code></td>
                  <td><span class="status-badge ok">✓ Valid (x0..x15)</span></td>
                  <td>Store lowest 8 bits of rs2 to memory address. LSU activates byte-enable strobe.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr data-cat="stores">
                  <td><code>sh rs2, offset(rs1)</code></td>
                  <td><span class="fmt-badge fmt-s">S-Type</span></td>
                  <td><code>0100011 (0x23)</code></td>
                  <td><code>001 (0x1)</code></td>
                  <td><code>imm[11:5|4:0]</code></td>
                  <td><code>Mem16[R[rs1] + sext(offset)] &larr; R[rs2][15:0]</code></td>
                  <td><span class="status-badge ok">✓ Valid (x0..x15)</span></td>
                  <td>Store lowest 16 bits of rs2 to memory address. LSU activates 2-byte lane strobes.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr data-cat="stores">
                  <td><code>sw rs2, offset(rs1)</code></td>
                  <td><span class="fmt-badge fmt-s">S-Type</span></td>
                  <td><code>0100011 (0x23)</code></td>
                  <td><code>010 (0x2)</code></td>
                  <td><code>imm[11:5|4:0]</code></td>
                  <td><code>Mem32[R[rs1] + sext(offset)] &larr; R[rs2][31:0]</code></td>
                  <td><span class="status-badge ok">✓ Valid (x0..x15)</span></td>
                  <td>Store full 32-bit word from rs2 into memory address. Activates all 4 byte strobes.</td>
                </tr>

                <!-- 3 System, Traps & Sync -->
                <tr data-cat="system">
                  <td><code>fence pred, succ</code></td>
                  <td><span class="fmt-badge fmt-i">I-Type</span></td>
                  <td><code>0001111 (0x0F)</code></td>
                  <td><code>000 (0x0)</code></td>
                  <td><code>fm[3:0] | pred[3:0] | succ[3:0]</code></td>
                  <td><code>Fence Memory &amp; Device I/O Access</code></td>
                  <td><span class="status-badge ok">✓ Valid (x0..x15)</span></td>
                  <td>Orders memory and memory-mapped device I/O accesses across predecessor and successor sets. Flushes LSU pipeline buffers.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr data-cat="system">
                  <td><code>ecall</code></td>
                  <td><span class="fmt-badge fmt-i">I-Type</span></td>
                  <td><code>1110011 (0x73)</code></td>
                  <td><code>000 (0x0)</code></td>
                  <td><code>imm[11:0] = 0x000</code></td>
                  <td><code>Trap: EnvironmentCall &rarr; mtvec</code></td>
                  <td><span class="status-badge ok">✓ Valid (x0..x15)</span></td>
                  <td>Generates synchronous trap to Machine Mode monitor or OS runtime (system call). Saves return PC in <code>mepc</code> and sets <code>mcause</code> to 11.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr data-cat="system">
                  <td><code>ebreak</code></td>
                  <td><span class="fmt-badge fmt-i">I-Type</span></td>
                  <td><code>1110011 (0x73)</code></td>
                  <td><code>000 (0x0)</code></td>
                  <td><code>imm[11:0] = 0x001</code></td>
                  <td><code>Trap: Breakpoint &rarr; Debugger</code></td>
                  <td><span class="status-badge ok">✓ Valid (x0..x15)</span></td>
                  <td>Transfers execution control back to interactive hardware debugger (JTAG/OpenOCD) or breakpoint exception handler (sets <code>mcause = 3</code>).</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Sub-part B: Standard Modular Extensions -->
      <div class="isa-subtopic-block" style="margin-bottom: 1.75rem;">
        <h4 class="isa-subtopic-title">
          <span class="pill-badge badge-teal">MODULAR EXTENSIONS</span>
          Silicon Cost vs. Software Benefit of Standard Extensions
        </h4>
        <p class="isa-subtopic-text">
          Once the base integer ISA is chosen, hardware architects selectively attach modular extensions. Each extension demands an explicit silicon area budget to unlock specific software speedups:
        </p>

        <div class="isa-extensions-flow">
          <!-- Extension M -->
          <div class="isa-ext-card">
            <div class="isa-ext-head">
              <div class="isa-ext-badge-group">
                <span class="isa-ext-badge badge-coral">EXTENSION 'M'</span>
                <span class="isa-ext-name">Integer Hardware Multiplication &amp; Division</span>
              </div>
              <div class="isa-cost-pill">Silicon Cost: +3.0 &ndash; 6.0 kGE (or 1&ndash;4 DSP Slices)</div>
            </div>
            <div class="isa-ext-body">
              <p>
                <strong>The Mechanism:</strong> Adds 8 instructions (<code>MUL</code>, <code>MULH</code>, <code>DIV</code>, <code>REM</code>, etc.). Hardware can range from a slow 34-cycle bit-serial shift-and-add circuit (PicoRV32), to an iterative Radix-4 divider (Ibex, SCR1), up to a fully-pipelined single-cycle multiplier (VeeR EL2).
              </p>
              <p>
                <strong>Software Payoff:</strong> <strong>15&times; to 35&times; acceleration</strong> over GCC software emulation routines (<code>__mulsi3</code>, <code>__divsi3</code>). Essential for digital filtering, motor control, and CoreMark benchmarking.
              </p>
              <div class="isa-adoption-note">
                <strong>Adoption Decision:</strong> Omitted in pure housekeeping cores (SERV) to preserve zero-silicon footprint; mandatory for compute &amp; control microcontrollers (Hazard3, SCR1, VeeR).
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Extension C -->
          <div class="isa-ext-card">
            <div class="isa-ext-head">
              <div class="isa-ext-badge-group">
                <span class="isa-ext-badge badge-lime">EXTENSION 'C'</span>
                <span class="isa-ext-name">Compressed 16-Bit Instructions (Code Density)</span>
              </div>
              <div class="isa-cost-pill">Silicon Cost: +600 &ndash; 1,200 Gates (Pre-decoder Logic)</div>
            </div>
            <div class="isa-ext-body">
              <p>
                <strong>The Mechanism:</strong> Re-encodes the most common 32-bit instructions (loads, stores, branches, integer arithmetic) into 16-bit equivalents. Requires a small 16-to-32-bit instruction expander in the Fetch/Decode stage and unaligned instruction fetch handling.
              </p>
              <p>
                <strong>The Memory Die Area Paradox:</strong> Reduces compiled firmware size by <strong>25% &ndash; 35%</strong>. In a microcontroller SoC, on-chip SRAM/ROM typically consumes <strong>60% to 80% of total silicon die area</strong>. Spending ~800 gates of core logic to shrink SRAM from 64 KB to 48 KB drastically reduces total chip cost!
              </p>
              <div class="isa-adoption-note">
                <strong>Adoption Decision:</strong> Virtually universal in commercial production MCUs (Ibex, NEORV32, Hazard3, SCR1, VeeR EL2).
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Extension B -->
          <div class="isa-ext-card">
            <div class="isa-ext-head">
              <div class="isa-ext-badge-group">
                <span class="isa-ext-badge badge-yellow">EXTENSION 'B'</span>
                <span class="isa-ext-name">Bit Manipulation (Zba, Zbb, Zbc, Zbs)</span>
              </div>
              <div class="isa-cost-pill">Silicon Cost: +1.5 &ndash; 3.0 kGE (ALU Additions)</div>
            </div>
            <div class="isa-ext-body">
              <p>
                <strong>The Mechanism:</strong> Accelerates bitwise operations: address generation (<code>Zba</code>: <code>sh1add</code>, <code>sh2add</code>), bitfield operations (<code>Zbb</code>: <code>clz</code>, <code>ctz</code>, <code>cpop</code>, <code>rol</code>, <code>ror</code>), carryless multiply (<code>Zbc</code>: CRC acceleration), and single-bit set/clear/extract (<code>Zbs</code>: <code>bset</code>, <code>bclr</code>, <code>binv</code>, <code>bext</code>).
              </p>
              <p>
                <strong>Software Payoff:</strong> Replaces 5 to 15 instructions of masking, shifting, and branching with a single 1-cycle instruction. Slashes cryptographic hashing, peripheral register bit-flipping, and CRC calculation overhead.
              </p>
              <div class="isa-adoption-note">
                <strong>Adoption Decision:</strong> Deployed in <strong>Hazard3</strong> (the RISC-V core in the Raspberry Pi RP2350 microcontroller) to deliver exceptional peripheral control and protocol processing.
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Extension A -->
          <div class="isa-ext-card">
            <div class="isa-ext-head">
              <div class="isa-ext-badge-group">
                <span class="isa-ext-badge badge-teal">EXTENSION 'A'</span>
                <span class="isa-ext-name">Atomic Memory Operations (AMO &amp; LR/SC)</span>
              </div>
              <div class="isa-cost-pill">Silicon Cost: +1.0 &ndash; 2.5 kGE + Bus Lock Hardware</div>
            </div>
            <div class="isa-ext-body">
              <p>
                <strong>The Mechanism:</strong> Provides Load-Reserved/Store-Conditional (<code>lr.w</code>/<code>sc.w</code>) and Atomic Read-Modify-Write instructions (<code>amoadd</code>, <code>amoswap</code>, etc.). Requires bus-level reservation monitors and exclusive bus transaction support.
              </p>
              <p>
                <strong>Software Payoff:</strong> Enables lock-free multi-threading, inter-process communication, and mutex primitives in multi-core SoCs or SMP operating systems.
              </p>
              <div class="isa-adoption-note">
                <strong>Adoption Decision:</strong> Unnecessary overhead in isolated single-core sensor controllers (PicoRV32, SERV); essential in Linux or multi-core environments (VexRiscv GenFull, NEORV32 multi-core).
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Extension Zfinx / F -->
          <div class="isa-ext-card">
            <div class="isa-ext-head">
              <div class="isa-ext-badge-group">
                <span class="isa-ext-badge badge-purple">EXTENSION 'Zfinx'</span>
                <span class="isa-ext-name">Floating-Point in Integer Registers</span>
              </div>
              <div class="isa-cost-pill">Silicon Cost: FPU Logic Only (Zero Extra RF Area)</div>
            </div>
            <div class="isa-ext-body">
              <p>
                <strong>The Mechanism:</strong> Standard <code>F</code> extension mandates 32 dedicated 32-bit floating-point registers (<code>f0 &ndash; f31</code>), doubling register file area and RTOS context-switch latency. <code>Zfinx</code> executes all IEEE-754 single-precision operations directly using the existing integer register file (<code>x0 &ndash; x31</code>).
              </p>
              <p>
                <strong>Software Payoff:</strong> Delivers true hardware IEEE-754 float acceleration for sensor fusion, PID motor loops, and audio DSP without paying the silicon penalty of a secondary register file.
              </p>
              <div class="isa-adoption-note">
                <strong>Adoption Decision:</strong> Supported by <strong>NEORV32</strong> and <strong>VexRiscv</strong> for embedded DSP applications where area is constrained.
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Privileged Architecture & PMP -->
          <div class="isa-ext-card">
            <div class="isa-ext-head">
              <div class="isa-ext-badge-group">
                <span class="isa-ext-badge badge-ink">PRIVILEGED &amp; PMP</span>
                <span class="isa-ext-name">Privileged Modes (M/U) &amp; Physical Memory Protection</span>
              </div>
              <div class="isa-cost-pill">Silicon Cost: +1.5 &ndash; 5.0 kGE (Comparators &amp; CSRs)</div>
            </div>
            <div class="isa-ext-body">
              <p>
                <strong>The Mechanism:</strong> Separates Machine Mode (<code>M</code>, baremetal supervisor) from User Mode (<code>U</code>, unprivileged app). Physical Memory Protection (PMP) implements programmable address checking registers (typically 4, 8, or 16 regions) that enforce Read/Write/Execute rules on every memory access.
              </p>
              <p>
                <strong>Hardware Security Payoff:</strong> Prevents buffer overflows or malicious code from accessing private cryptographic keys or critical peripheral control registers. Enables hardware roots-of-trust and isolated enclaves.
              </p>
              <div class="isa-adoption-note">
                <strong>Adoption Decision:</strong> Central to <strong>Ibex</strong> in Google's OpenTitan silicon root-of-trust, combined with Dual-Core Lockstep (DCLS) for fault detection.
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Sub-part C: Cross-Core Architectural Decision Matrix -->
      <div class="isa-subtopic-block">
        <h4 class="isa-subtopic-title">
