        <!-- 2.2.2 NEORV32 DEEP-DIVE -->
        <div class="sub-topic-card" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
          <div class="sub-topic-head">
            <div class="sub-topic-title-group">
              <span class="pill-badge badge-teal">CORE 5</span>
              <h4 class="sub-topic-title">NEORV32 &bull; 2-Stage Modular SoC</h4>
            </div>
            <span class="sub-topic-spec-badge">~24.5 kGE</span>
          </div>
          <p>
            Authored by Stephan Nolting in highly readable, standard-compliant <strong>VHDL-93</strong>, <strong>NEORV32</strong> is an exemplary open-source microcontroller system-on-chip that has gained widespread adoption across academic labs and industrial FPGA projects:
          </p>
          <ul class="concept-list">
            <li><strong>Clean 2-Stage Pipelined Architecture:</strong> Like Ibex, NEORV32 overlaps instruction fetch with decode/execution. The core is completely synchronous and free from vendor-specific FPGA primitives, allowing it to synthesize seamlessly on Xilinx, Intel/Altera, Lattice, Microchip, and Gowin devices.</li>
            <li><strong>Wishbone b4 Pipelined Interconnect:</strong> Features a standardized 32-bit pipelined Wishbone b4 bus interface with configurable latency and burst capabilities, making it trivial to integrate custom memory-mapped peripherals.</li>
            <li><strong>Tightly-Coupled Memories (IMEM &amp; DMEM):</strong> Incorporates internal dual-port block RAMs for deterministic single-cycle access to real-time code and stack frames, bypassing external bus contention.</li>
            <li><strong>Extensive Extension Support:</strong> Supports RV32I/E with optional M (multiplication/division), C (compressed 16-bit instructions), A (atomic operations), B (bit manipulation), and custom coprocessor extensions (CFU) for domain-specific algorithmic acceleration.</li>
          </ul>

