            <h5 class="verdict-title">&#9878; System Architect's Decision Guide: When to Select Archetype 2?</h5>
            <ul class="concept-list">
              <li><strong>Select Ibex when:</strong> You are designing a commercial ASIC or secure SoC requiring silicon-proven reliability, formal verification heritage, native Open Bus Interface (OBI) integration, or advanced hardware security hardening (OpenTitan root-of-trust, DCLS dual-core lockstep).</li>
              <li><strong>Select NEORV32 when:</strong> You are deploying on FPGAs and require an out-of-the-box complete microcontroller SoC in pure VHDL-93, with native Wishbone peripherals (UART, SPI, TMR, I2C), bootloader, and custom instruction extension (CFU) capabilities.</li>
              <li><strong>Avoid Archetype 2 when:</strong> Your design requires clock frequencies above 400 MHz in standard cell silicon or sustained CPI &lt; 1.0, where deep pipelining (Archetype 3) or superscalar dual-issue (Archetype 4) becomes necessary.</li>
            </ul>
