          <!-- Architectural Decision Guide -->
          <div class="arch-verdict-box" style="margin-top: 1.25rem;">
            <h5 class="verdict-title">&#9878; System Architect's Decision Guide: When to Select Archetype 3?</h5>
            <ul class="concept-list">
              <li><strong>Select Hazard3 when:</strong> Your SoC design requires clock frequencies above 400 MHz in standard CMOS nodes, native dual AHB5 bus interfaces, fast 16-cycle hardware division, and commercial silicon verification (RP2350).</li>
              <li><strong>Select VexRiscv when:</strong> You are targeting high-end FPGAs (Xilinx UltraScale, Intel Stratix) and require a mature, modular 5-stage RISC architecture with dynamic BTB branch prediction, instruction/data caches, and MMU support for Linux.</li>
              <li><strong>Avoid Archetype 3 when:</strong> You cannot afford the silicon area for full forwarding multiplexers and dual-ported SRAMs, where a simpler 2-stage core (Archetype 2) delivers adequate performance at 40% lower gate count.</li>
